    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.47), our two premier offensive engines. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez, whose 4.70 xERA provides the right environment for his high-base projection, compounded further by the hitter-friendly park factor (+16%) and a strong order position. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-ceiling platoon advantage against Carlos Rod\u00f3n, with the batting order and SP skill metrics coalescing to make him a must-start staple. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) is our most interesting high-upside play; while he faces a decent pitcher in Bailey Ober, his elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides an intrinsic boost to our stolen base aspirations, a category we continue to prioritize aggressively.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Miguel Vargas** (47.01) on the bench. He was the final cut for our utility spot, ultimately sidelined by a sub-optimal matchup against McLean\u2014whose 3.61 xERA is the toughest hurdle among our primary considerations today\u2014and a slightly lower efficiency ceiling compared to our starting infielders. We continue to monitor **Nasim Nunez** (56.79), whose efficiency remains in the marginal tier; while he offers high-speed upside, the 8th-order slot suppresses his potential for counting stats. Investors should be aware that while **Kyle Tucker** (58.73) remains in the lineup, his lower-than-average SP skill score is a byproduct of the matchup against Bachar, yet he remains in the start column due to his high daily floor. We are fortunate that our injury report for **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remains unchanged, allowing us to focus our full attention on maximizing current active-roster efficiency.",
